---
import Page from '../layouts/Page.astro';
import PhoneButton from '../components/PhoneButton.astro';
import TeamGrid from '../components/TeamGrid.astro';
import { agent, brand, licenses, links, nameableIn } from '../config/site';
const approved = nameableIn('FL');
---
<Page
  title={`About ${brand.name}`}
  h1={`About ${brand.name}`}
  description="Who we are, how we work, our licenses and exactly how we're paid. An independent final expense insurance agency in Florida."
  path="/about/"
  crumb="About us"
  updated="2026-11-06"
>
  <p class="lede">
    {brand.name} is an independent life insurance agency in {brand.region}. We help families find final expense coverage they can afford, and we
    explain it in plain English or Spanish.
  </p>
  <p>(TODO: 2–3 sentences on why the agency exists and a real example of a family we helped, shared with permission or anonymized. First-hand experience matters here.)</p>

  <h2>Who you'll talk to</h2>
  <p>Every call is with a licensed agent. Check any of our licenses yourself with <a href={links.dfsLookup} rel="noopener">Florida DFS</a>.</p>
  <TeamGrid />

  <h2>Our licenses</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Florida insurance agency license <strong>{brand.agencyLicenseNumber}</strong></li>
    <li>Agent in charge: Florida resident life insurance agent license <strong>{agent.flLicense}</strong>, National Producer Number (NPN) <strong>{agent.npn}</strong></li>
    <li>Agent licensed in: {licenses.map((l) => l.name).join(', ')}. <a href="/licenses/">See every license</a>.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    You can check any license yourself with the <a href={links.dfsLookup} rel="noopener">Florida Department of Financial Services</a> or{' '}
    <a href={links.nipr} rel="noopener">NIPR</a>. Please do, before you share personal details with anyone.
  </p>

  <h2>How we work</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>We're an <strong>independent agency</strong>, not part of one insurance company. We're appointed with several insurers{approved.length ? ` (${approved.map((c) => c.shortName).join(', ')})` : ''}, so we can compare their plans for you.</li>
    <li>Most of our work happens <strong>by phone</strong>, and every call is with a licensed agent. Many insurers accept applications by phone and give a decision during the call.</li>
    <li>We'll never pressure you to decide on the first call, and we'll tell you if a plan has a waiting period.</li>
    <li>If we can't help, for example because you live in a state where we're not licensed, we'll say so.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>How we're paid</h2>
  <p>
    The insurance company pays us a commission when a policy is issued. You don't pay us anything. Insurers set their own prices, so buying
    through us doesn't change your premium. Commissions differ between insurers and plan types; we recommend the plan that fits your health and
    budget, and we'll explain why.
  </p>

  <h2>An agency, not an insurer</h2>
  <p>{brand.name} is an independent insurance agency, not an insurance company. Your policy is issued by the insurer named on it.</p>

  <div class="btn-row"><PhoneButton label="Call us" location="about" /></div>
</Page>
